// Reactivity S5 (hardening) — one effect can subscribe to several signals at once (the complement of a
// fan-out: many sources into one subscriber). This effect reads `a`, `b`, and `c`; it runs once on
// creation, and a change to *any* of the three reruns it exactly once, seeing the current value of all
// three. Each set is an independent dependency, so all three edges are live simultaneously.
// expect: stdout "sum=6"
// expect: stdout "sum=16"
// expect: stdout "sum=26"
// expect: stdout "sum=36"
// expect: exit 0
a = signal(1)
b = signal(2)
c = signal(3)
effect(fn() {
    echo "sum=${a.get() + b.get() + c.get()}"
})
a.set(11)
b.set(12)
c.set(13)
